# Encryption key for API key storage (required)
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
ENCRYPTION_KEY=change-me-to-a-random-secret

# Directory for the local file-backed data store shared between the browser
# and the MCP server (optional, defaults to ./.ayu-data)
# AYU_DATA_DIR=./.ayu-data

# GitHub OAuth App Client ID, used for the "Sign in with GitHub" Device Flow
# in Integrations. Optional — test-lah ships with its own registered OAuth
# App by default (see src/lib/github/deviceFlow.ts), so Device Flow works
# out of the box for npm installs with no setup. Set this only if you're
# self-hosting from source and want to use your own OAuth App instead (e.g.
# a private fork, or your org's own registration). Device flow needs only a
# Client ID — no client secret and no fixed callback URL, since this app can
# run on any local host/port per install and device flow authenticates the
# device, not a redirect target. Register a new OAuth App at
# https://github.com/settings/developers, enable "Device Flow" in its
# settings, and paste the Client ID here (the Authorization callback URL can
# be set to anything, e.g. http://localhost, since it's never used).
# GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
